{"seq":23,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"fact","id":"f06484"},"reason":"a1297 f06484: bodyEn: \"„Purple Rain“, both the movie and its title ballad, were written by the Minneapolis musician himself; the film opened in American cinemas on 27 July 1984, the soundtrack album spent 24 weeks at number one in the United States and the film won the Oscar for Best Original Song Score.\" → \"Albert Magnoli directed the film from a script by Magnoli and William Blinn built on Prince's own ideas, but every song of „Purple Rain“, including the title ballad, was written by Prince himself; the film opened in American cinemas on 27 July 1984, the soundtrack album spent 24 weeks at number one in the United States and Prince won the Oscar for Best Original Song Score.\" — the screenplay was by Albert Magnoli and William Blinn, not Prince; the Oscar went to Prince, not the film — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple_Rain_(film)","by":"enrich batch 132","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a1297-a1657.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple_Rain_(film"}]},
